### MILESTONE: GPU-to-GPU Cross-Device Copy WORKS!
```
cuda:0->cuda:1: [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]   <- LOCAL → REMOTE
cuda:1->cuda:0: [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]   <- REMOTE → LOCAL
=== ALL CPU-GPU AND GPU-GPU OFFLOAD TESTS PASSED ===
```
Root cause: PyTorch's `copy_device_to_device` uses `cudaMemcpyAsync(D2D)` with UVA,
but local/remote pointers are on different machines. Fixed by intercepting D2D memcpy
when src/dst are on different devices (via pointer-to-device tracker), staging through CPU.

Also fixed: cudaDeviceCanAccessPeer (was sending RPC with invalid device nums),
CUDA event routing (events created on wrong device), cudaStreamWaitEvent (context
deactivation + remote event handles), cudaEventRecordWithFlags (missing interception).

